# Example: let-bindings in a method

Intermediate names are immutable. The last statement is the result.

## Schema

```
Game = PlayArea Ball
PlayArea = Rect
Rect = Int/x Int/y Int/width Int/height
Ball = Int/x Int/y Int/dx Int/dy Int/rad
```

## Construction

```
[:Game
  [:PlayArea [0 0 800 600]]
  [:Ball 100 100 1 1 5]
]
```

## Methods

```
Ball::move = {
  nx = x + dx.
  ny = y + dy.
  [:Ball nx ny dx dy rad]
}

Rect::area = {
  a = width * height.
  a
}
```

## Target

```
%main
public static function main():Void {
    var assemblage = gameFactory();
    var helper = new WCHNTHelper();
    trace(assemblage.toConstruction(0, helper));
}
```
